00:00:00,580 --> 00:00:02,270
B2.

2
00:00:02,270 --> 00:00:07,870
Amy and Daniel are talking about how to stay safe in emergencies.

3
00:00:07,870 --> 00:00:13,125
Listen to their conversation and complete the notes below.

4
00:00:13,125 --> 00:00:17,920
There was some really good advice in that talk.

5
00:00:17,920 --> 00:00:20,900
But what about emergencies?

6
00:00:20,900 --> 00:00:25,750
What should we do if we get caught in an emergency?

7
00:00:25,750 --> 00:00:33,190
Well, if your building is on fire, try to get out as soon as possible.

8
00:00:33,190 --> 00:00:43,570
Cover your mouth and nose with a wet piece of cloth to protect yourself from thick smoke and stay low to the ground.

9
00:00:43,570 --> 00:00:51,530
If it is impossible for you to get out, find a safe place to stay and wait for help.

10
00:00:51,530 --> 00:00:57,250
Yes, and don't go back into a building on fire.

11
00:00:57,250 --> 00:00:59,620
It's very dangerous.

12
00:00:59,620 --> 00:01:02,690
Yes, that's really important.

13
00:01:02,690 --> 00:01:09,700
And car accidents happen every day, so what should we do if we see one?

14
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:15,180
I think we should make an emergency call as soon as possible.

15
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:20,880
Then we can check if people in the cars are fine or not.

16
00:01:20,880 --> 00:01:25,230
Remember not to move them if they are badly hurt.

17
00:01:25,230 --> 00:01:27,480
That's useful advice.

18
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:36,590
I think it's also important to put emergency signs around the cars or other accidents might happen.
